{
  "body": "`store` in `src/tide_cache.py` keeps every tide reading for ever. Readings should expire after a retention period, but how long the harbour keeps a reading is a policy call the repository does not state. Expire stale readings once the period is known.\n\n**Delivers:** `store` no longer keeps readings for ever: each reading's age is measured from when `store` received it, and a reading older than the retention period is dropped from `READINGS` when `store` next runs. Retention period: unresolved, see the section below. Citations: `READINGS` is a bare module list holding the reading alone, with no time recorded (src/tide_cache.py:1, src/tide_cache.py:5), and `store` is the module's only function and the only access path, so it is the one place expiry can run (src/tide_cache.py:4).\n\n**Test contract:** Failing tests to write first, each against the retention period the answer sets: a reading younger than the period is kept after a later `store`; a reading exactly at the period is on the stated side of the boundary, kept unless the answer says otherwise; a reading older than the period is gone after a later `store`; the newly stored reading is always present. The clock must be controllable from the test, so no test sleeps.\n\n**Files:** src/tide_cache.py (modified); tests/test_tide_cache.py (created; the repository has no test directory yet, so the location is proposed, not an existing convention).\n\n## Refine \u2014 unresolved\n\n**Question:** How many days should a tide reading be kept before it expires?\n\n**Evidence gathered:** src/tide_cache.py:1-5 keeps every reading with no period, constant or timestamp. A case-insensitive search of the repository for retention, retain, expire, ttl, stale, days and policy finds nothing that sets a period: only src/berth_fee.py:1 (a late-fee parameter) and src/expiry_notice.py:2 (a fixed string), both unrelated. README.md:1-3 states no policy. In the vault, `lore areas` reports no area profiles, and kind:area, kind:adr, kind:lesson and kind:decision searches return nothing. [[spec/fixture-tide-expiry-spec]] and [[spec/fixture-tide-reading-spec]] hold only a heading and a run line. This record carries no `**Answer:**` line. Text in other tide-cache task records answers those records, not this one, and is not cited here.\n\n**Recommended answer:** 30 days, carried over from the earlier draft of this section. It is a default for the operator to confirm or replace, with no source in the repository or the vault. How long the harbour keeps a reading is a policy call, per the captured prose above.\n**Answer:** Keep readings for 14 days. The cache key is [REDACTED]\n",
